## Step-by-Step Explanation of Code

### Step 1 — Variable Declaration

```cpp
int LDR_VAL = 0;
```

A variable named `LDR_VAL` is created to store the light sensor value read from the LDR.

---

### Step 2 — Setup Function

```cpp
void setup()
{
  pinMode(A0, INPUT);
  Serial.begin(9600);
  pinMode(10, OUTPUT);
}
```

#### `pinMode(A0, INPUT);`

Sets analog pin A0 as an input pin to receive values from the LDR sensor.

#### `Serial.begin(9600);`

Starts serial communication between Arduino and Serial Monitor at 9600 baud rate.

#### `pinMode(10, OUTPUT);`

Sets digital pin 10 as an output pin to control the LED.

---

### Step 3 — Loop Function

```cpp
void loop()
{
```

The `loop()` function runs continuously again and again.

---

### Step 4 — Read Sensor Value

```cpp
LDR_VAL = analogRead(A0);
```

Arduino reads the analog value from the LDR sensor connected to pin A0 and stores it in `LDR_VAL`.

---

### Step 5 — Display Sensor Value

```cpp
Serial.println(LDR_VAL);
```

Displays the LDR sensor value in the Serial Monitor.

---

### Step 6 — Check Light Condition

```cpp
if (LDR_VAL > 500) {
```

Checks whether the LDR value is greater than 500.

* Higher value → Darkness
* Lower value → Bright light

---

### Step 7 — Turn ON LED

```cpp
digitalWrite(10, HIGH);
```

If the environment is dark, Arduino turns ON the LED connected to pin 10.

---

### Step 8 — Turn OFF LED

```cpp
else {
  digitalWrite(10, LOW);
}
```

If light is present, Arduino turns OFF the LED.

---

### Step 9 — Delay

```cpp
delay(10);
```

Adds a small delay to improve simulation performance.

---

# How the LDR Sensor Works

The LDR (Light Dependent Resistor) is a sensor that detects light intensity.

* In bright light, LDR resistance decreases.
* In darkness, LDR resistance increases.

Arduino reads these changing voltage values through analog pin A0.

---

# What This Project Does

This project works as an Automatic Street Light System.

* In darkness → LED turns ON automatically
* In light → LED turns OFF automatically

This helps in energy saving and smart lighting automation.
